Description: Hi.

I have pretty simple code to compare express route parameters (wich uses "router" package) and path-match, both use path-to-regexp under the hood.
```javascript
import Pathmatch from 'path-match'

const routeMatch = Pathmatch({
	sensitive: false,
	strict: false,
	// end: false
})('/api/:module/:s*');

app.get('/api/:module/:s*', (req, res) => {
	const pr = {};
	pr['srv'] = req.params;
	pr['lib'] = routeMatch(req.path);

	res.json(pr);
});
```
and i get strange results with path "/api/about/first/second":

```
{
  "srv":{
    "0": "/second",
    "module": "about",
    "s":"first"
  },
  "lib":{
    "module": "about",
    "s":["first","second"]
  }
}
```
Also express doesnt handle path "/api/about" in that case.
Thats a bug or my missunderstanding of concepts?

--
